From aee2589e6d54a06a21cc0df9ecb1f4bff8bb15ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 17:33:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dashboard: radio-count-driven (support quad-band BE98, keep
 tri-band BE96U)

Make Main_ReaperDash.asp render an arbitrary radio count instead of a
hardcoded 2.4/5/6 triple. Emit wl0..wl3, filter radios with no nband
(BE96U keeps 3, BE98 keeps 4), assign a stable index and a band label
that disambiguates two radios on the same band ('5 GHz (2)'). Radio
tiles and per-radio MAC rows are generated from the WL[] list and keyed
by radio index; MWL fronthaul SSID/MAC are matched by band bitmask.
Client band-bars are unchanged (already band-aggregated via isWL).

Shared UI change; carried on both BE98 branches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
